{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1221515-test-drive-karma","id":1221515,"title":"Test drive: Karma","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-23T12:03:03-07:00","id":1221515,"title":"Test drive: Karma","content":"New idea for a karma mechanic:<br /> <br /> Virtue and Vice refill willpower per normal. Indulging virtue provides a positive karma dot and vice provides a negative karma dot. 4 karma points maximum can accrue but do not expire until used. At any time the storyteller may choose a characters roll to either apply a bonus using a positive karma point or apply a negative using the negative connotation. Applying a positive karma point grants the eight or nine again quality And grants an exceptional success at three instead of five. Applying the negative karma point reduces the roll to a chance dice.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T14:47:04-07:00","id":1221549,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly not really seeing the point of it.<br /> <br /> It just seems like an excessive thing to track, that exists to let the ST have more control over the player's character. Why would a player want to engage with this over the natural 2e Condition cycle?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:39:08-07:00","id":1221574,"title":"","content":"This also disincentivizes Vice.<br /> <br /> I'd abstract it out - when the characters act good, give the ST a point that they can cash in for a temporary dot in Allies, Contacts, Resources, etc. or (a few points for) a narrative turn of good fortune, like an ally turning up to save you in a fight.<br /> <br /> For acting like an a-hole, the ST gets a point to throw complication at the PCs, like an NPC hearing about them and having a worse disposition, or an enemy showing up at exactly the wrong time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T18:51:18-07:00","id":1221589,"title":"","content":"Virtue and Vice intentionally have different opportunity costs. A character who goes all in on Virtue at all opportunities, and shuns her Vice completely, will take awhile to accumulate four points of positive karma, whereas a character who does the opposite will likely hit four points of negative karma within a single session.<br /> <br /> Vice is not intended to be a trap; characters who shun all opportunities to satisfy their Vice are forsaking an important source of Willpower. (A resource which is used primarily to boost dice pools, incidentally, which is overshadowed by the magnitude of the penalty incurred by a point of negative karma.)<br /> <br /> Vice is not always immoral; indulging a Vice need not cause material harm, and Vices like Impatient or Lazy can reflect personal weaknesses rather than inclinations toward immorality.<br /> <br /> The genre of the default Chronicles of Darkness game is not a cosmically just world where good is consistently rewarded and evil punished. This is the least important criticism. As long as you know you're consciously deviating from the default, there's nothing wrong with doing that. But the above points still apply..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 05-23-2018, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T02:38:59-07:00","id":1221637,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, precisely because this works on the assumption of morality tied to Vice and Virtue, I\u2019d add some sort of \u201cgain more supernatural power\u201d to negative Karma, and incorporate it to (yet another) Inferno 2E conversion. (And likely associate Karma with control over/by the Possessing demon, instead of dice tricks)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}